{"author":{"id":"89da5fec8eff6d69dbcdd68f81be7e9163b16f34b17e978ecf3554487379f453"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1773097567,"nonce":"4i1I8WEHzTZCeDYGxvhZZcbxUQU=","title":"settings: dualWriteReaperConf regex misses bare VAR= lines, causing duplicate entries","message":"dualWriteReaperConf() uses regex ^(export\\s+VAR=).*$ which does not match existing bare VAR=value lines in ~/.config/claude-reaper/config. Result: both the old line and a new export VAR=\"value\" line exist. Later line wins when sourced so behavior is correct, but messy and confusing. Fix: broaden regex to match both forms, keeping export format in replacement.","files":null}]}